hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17100","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Muhammad ibn Yazid, that Abdullah ibn Awf narrated to him that Abu Jum'ah Habib ibn Siba' - and he had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in the year of the Confederates, prayed Maghrib, and when he finished, he said: Does any of you know that I prayed Asr? They said: O Messenger of Allah, you did not pray it. So he ordered the mu'adhdhin, and he gave iqamah for prayer, and he prayed Asr, then he repeated Maghrib."
"17101","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: Usayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said: Salih Abu Muhammad narrated to me, he said: Abu Jumah narrated to me, he said: We had lunch with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and with us was Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. He said: He said: O Messenger of Allah, is anyone better than us? We accepted Islam with you and strove in jihad with you. He said: Yes, a people who will come after you, believing in me though they never saw me."
"17102","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: Usayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Durayk, from Abu Muhayriz, he said: I said to Abu Jumah, a man of the Companions: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Yes, I will narrate to you a good hadith. We had lunch with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and with us was Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is anyone better than us? We accepted Islam with you and strove in jihad with you. He said: Yes, a people who will come after you, believing in me though they never saw me."
